        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">For B2B procurement managers sourcing thermal refrigerants, MOQs are rarely arbitrary sales quotas—they are hard breakeven thresholds driven by blow-mold tooling, rotogravure printing, and chemical batch minimums. Understanding these three factory cost drivers lets you budget tooling CAPEX accurately, avoid sampling delays, and align inventory with cold chain launches. </p>
