    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight mb-4 [text-wrap:balance]">
      Custom Cold Pack MOQ: Tooling, Sampling, and Lead Time for B2B Buyers
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
      For B2B procurement managers sourcing thermal refrigerants, Minimum Order Quantities (MOQs) reflect real factory economics rather than arbitrary sales quotas. They represent hard breakeven thresholds tied to mold cavitation, rotogravure printing cylinders, and chemical batch minimums. Understanding these three drivers helps buyers budget tooling capital, schedule validation runs, and align delivery with seasonal cold chain launches.
    </p>
  </header>

  <img
    src="https://yourdomain.com/images/blog-image-1.webp"
    alt="Blow-molded HDPE phase-change bricks and custom-printed flexible gel packs arranged on an OEM cold chain inspection line"
