  <section class="pt-8 border-t border-slate-200">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-4 mb-6">
      Frequently Asked Questions for B2B Cold Pack Buyers
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          1. Who retains legal ownership of custom blow molds and printing cylinders?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          When you pay 100% of a custom CNC mold or rotogravure cylinder invoice, full tooling ownership remains yours. Include a signed NNN (Non-Disclosure, Non-Use, Non-Circumvention) agreement barring the factory from running your tooling for third parties and requiring climate-protected storage between orders.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          2. Are custom tooling and sampling fees refundable on bulk production orders?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Pre-production sample fees ($150–$400 plus air courier) are routinely credited toward your first bulk purchase order. Custom blow-mold fees ($3,500–$8,500) are normally billed upfront and amortized once cumulative orders reach 50,000–100,000 units, while engraved printing cylinders are stored free for repeat runs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          3. Can we split one MOQ across different temperature ratings (e.g., 0°C and -20°C)?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Yes, if both variants share the exact same HDPE shell mold and color. Factories can split the run across two coolants provided each PCM fill meets its reactor mixing minimum (typically 1,000–2,000 pcs per temperature rating). Printed gel pouches can share base film and differentiate temperatures via waterproof labels.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          4. How long does factory sampling take, and what QA tests are included?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Stock-mold samples ship in 5–7 days; custom-printed gel packs take 10–15 days; and T1 custom blow-mold samples take 25–35 days. Confirm your supplier performs a 72-hour freeze-thaw leak check, a 1.2-meter frozen drop test, and 50–80 kg static compression testing before dispatch.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          5. What is the shelf life if we warehouse 20,000 custom gel packs to meet MOQ?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Unused PA/PE laminated gel packs and HDPE bricks store safely at ambient temperatures (10°C–30°C, out of direct sunlight) for 24 to 36 months. Buyers with limited pallet space can also negotiate printing the full film roll upfront while scheduling two staggered filling and shipping batches.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          6. What compliance documents should accompany custom cold pack samples?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Request up-to-date Material Safety Data Sheets (MSDS), IATA/IMDG non-hazardous air and ocean transport certificates, and food-contact polymer declarations during sampling. For pharmaceutical lanes, also review the lab’s DSC thermogram verifying latent heat capacity (J/g) and exact phase-change stability.
        </p>

        
